WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.890
The Umbrella Academy was a breakout hit for
Netflix, pulling in viewers and generating

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.640
buzz on its debut in early 2019.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.260
It's no surprise that the show is returning
for a second season, especially considering

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.340
the cliffhanger that closed the first.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.940
But what can we expect when the Academy comes
back?

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:21.940
Right now, there's no official release date
for the second season of The Umbrella Academy,

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.460
but we do know one is coming.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.500
When can we expect it?

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.660
Well, we have a theory.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:31.260
In January 2018, comic creators Gerard Way
and Gabriel Bá shared a picture from the

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.700
first day of production.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.060
The show itself premiered just over a year
later, in February 2019.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.840
Season 2 got underway in June 2019.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.839
If we take the first season as a model, that
means we can hopefully expect season two somewhere

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.840
in the second half of 2020.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.440
“I don't know, do you have a better idea?"

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:52.980
Obviously, it's not a perfect estimate.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:57.519
We'll have an update when we get an official
word, but fans can probably pencil in "late

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.440
2020" until further notice.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.880
All of Reginald Hargreeves' children will
be back for the second season, played by the

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:04.800
same actors.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:10.530
The official Twitter account for The Umbrella
Academy shared a video on June 15th, 2019,

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:13.119
showing the first script reading for the second
season.

00:01:13.119 --> 00:01:17.729
We knew that the entire principal cast was
returning for the second season of Umbrella

00:01:17.729 --> 00:01:21.040
Academy, but we've been in the dark as to
what newbies might be coming aboard.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:25.740
No longer in September, Netflix announced
the three new cast members that we will see

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:30.960
in the show's second season: Yusuf Gatewood,
Marin Ireland, and Ritu Arya.

00:01:31.229 --> 00:01:35.420
Gatewood was recently seen as Famine, one
of the four horsemen, in Amazon Prime's Good

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:36.620
Omens adaptation.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:41.460
In Umbrella Academy, he will play Raymond,
who Netflix describes as "a charismatic born

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:41.960
leader."

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:46.440
If you remember Famine's smooth talking from
Good Omens, that sounds perfectly suited for

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:46.940
Gatewood.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:51.360
Ireland, who will play Sissy, has dozens of
credits to her name, but Sneaky Pete is the

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.249
one most likely to ring some bells.

00:01:53.249 --> 00:01:58.000
Arya will play Lila, described in a press
release as "a chameleon, who can be as brilliant

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.170
or insane as the situation requires."

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:05.000
She has appeared in several BBC shows, as
well as the AMC series Humans.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:09.600
Interestingly, none of these characters have
appeared in the Umbrella Academy comics at

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:10.600
least, not yet.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:14.720
Even with these announcements, we're still
in the dark about where season 2's story is

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:15.220
headed.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:19.260
We also don't know which other major players
from the first season might be back.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:24.180
Time-traveling assassins Cha-Cha and Hazel
had significant roles in the first season,

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:27.100
as did Reginald Hargreeves, Agnes, and The
Handler.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:31.240
We could very well see some of them again,
but due to the events of the finale, none

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:36.120
of these characters would be absolutely essential
in carrying the second season's plot forward.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:40.360
"I'm done with all this madness; time to start
over."

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:45.560
The end of The Umbrella Academy's first season
saw most of our siblings joining together

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:50.370
to try to stop their sister, Vanya, in her
full, badass "White Violin" persona, from

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.890
bringing about the apocalypse.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:56.720
They... did not succeed, with their efforts
to stop Vanya inadvertently sending a wave

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:58.140
of energy towards the moon.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:02.640
Pieces of the moon began to rain down, destroying
the world just as the siblings jumped back

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:03.140
in time.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:07.460
This ending differs a bit from the first volume
of the comic, but it followed the same basic

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:07.960
path.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.460
It seems likely that season two will at least
draw inspiration from the second volume of

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.640
the comic, "Dallas."

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:19.180
This story deals with the Academy trying to
assassinate JFK in order to prevent the apocalypse…

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:19.680
somehow.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:23.820
Considering they were unable to stop the world
from ending at the end of the first season,

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:27.840
traveling back in time and giving it another
go seems like a fairly solid plan.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:33.220
However, the story going forward may deviate
from the comics the first episode of the second

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.560
season is titled "Right Back Where We Started."

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:39.290
So while it seems a given that the siblings
are going back to the past, when it comes

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:41.560
to where exactly, we'll have to wait and see.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.920
The Umbrella Academy's first season was a
huge hit for Netflix.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:50.180
As long as it keeps people tuned to the streaming
platform, Netflix will probably find a way

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:54.540
to keep financing the show and there's a lot
of comic material to keep them going.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:59.000
In an interview with The Hollywood Reporter,
Gerard Way and showrunner Steve Blackman talked

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.280
about the planned story.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:04.290
Way said that he has eight volumes of comic
stories planned, and that Blackman has an

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.100
outline of major plot points.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:10.930
However, the first season of the show drew
elements from both the first and second volumes,

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:15.040
so a "one volume equals one season" formula
doesn't necessarily work here.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:20.040
The publication schedule of the Umbrella Academy
comics has been a bit all over the place.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:25.000
The first issue was released in 2007, with
the first two volumes, "Apocalypse Suite"

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.440
and "Dallas," collected in their entirety
by the end of 2008.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:33.180
The third and, to date, final collected Umbrella
Academy story is "Hotel Oblivion."

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:37.600
Despite its announcement immediately after
the conclusion of Dallas, Hotel Oblivion didn't

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.000
begin publication until 2018.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.580
So, why the long delay?

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:45.340
"The world is changing — has changed."

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:50.960
Comic creator Gerard Way is also a musician,
best known for his work with My Chemical Romance.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:56.340
Though the band broke up in 2013, he has remained
busy with solo work, and he's also written

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:58.080
numerous other comic book projects.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:01.200
But that doesn't mean he's abandoned The Umbrella
Academy story.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.340
Way told The Hollywood Reporter that he is
planning on eight volumes, and he hopes that

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.140
the comics can stay ahead of the show.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:12.090
Speaking to Radio Times, Way said that the
overall goal is, basically, to not fall into

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:13.710
the trap that hit Game of Thrones.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:14.710
As he put it,

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:18.870
"The goal for us is to stay ahead of the show
and since we're on series three [of the comics],

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:20.200
we are now ahead of the show."

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:24.540
While we wait for a second season of the show,
we can likely expect to start hearing news

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.620
about the fourth volume of the books.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:27.620
According to Way,

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:31.800
“The idea with the comic is to go right
from series three, take a three-to-four-month

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.110
break, then go right into series four.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:36.060
[...] There is story there and it’s all
planned out.”

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:40.680
Obviously, the most logical prediction about
where The Umbrella Academy's second season

00:05:40.681 --> 00:05:43.180
is headed would be the JFK assassination.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:47.340
However, there are plenty of other mysteries
from the pages of the books that the show

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:48.100
could turn to.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:52.180
The show touched on it, but a little more
backstory about Sir Reginald would be nice

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:56.800
especially considering that, in the comics,
we're told that he's an alien almost immediately.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.560
The last episode of the first season gave
some hints towards this, but never really

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:01.300
addressed it.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:05.760
Along those lines, that revelation would also
raise another obvious question: what about

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:07.400
all the other mystery children?

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:12.360
There are supposedly 42 of them, and Reginald
enlisted seven to begin his Academy.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.580
Season 2 could certainly catch up with some
of those other kids.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:19.760
The other looming possibility is the Hotel
Oblivion and, specifically, the character

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:20.760
of John Perseus.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:25.780
The new season will need a good villain, and
Perseus seems a likely candidate, especially

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:29.820
if he works more in the background of the
second season before becoming an even bigger

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.080
threat in season 3.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:35.680
The Umbrella Academy has dealt with other
villains, but Perseus seems like the best

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:36.700
bet for television.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:40.580
So while the comics can give us hints about
where the story of the show is going, the

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:44.660
only way we'll know for sure what happens
is to wait and watch season two unfold.

